    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] Ceredigion, formerly \"Cardiganshire\", is a constituency represented in the House of Commons of the Parliament of the United Kingdom.\n[2] Officially, the full name of the house is: the Honourable the Commons of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland in Parliament assembled.\n[3] Ross and Cromarty was a county constituency of the House of Commons of the Parliament of the United Kingdom from 1832 to 1983.\n[4] The Ross and Cromarty by-election, 1936 was a parliamentary by-election for the British House of Commons constituency of Ross and Cromarty held on 10 February 1936."
